City
means the Corporation of the City of Waterloo;
City solicitor
means the City Solicitor, or anyone designated by the City Solicitor to perform his or her duties pursuant to this bylaw;
Clerk
means the City Clerk, or anyone designated by the City Clerk to perform his or her duties pursuant to this bylaw;
Council
means the elected Council of the City;
Dangerous dog bylaw
means bylaw No. 2026-010 passed by the City to regulate dangerous dogs, potentially dangerous dogs and prohibited dogs in the City, as amended from time to time, or any successor thereof;
Director
means the Director of Municipal Enforcement Services, or their designate;
Designated bylaw
means any provision of a City bylaw to which the parking administrative penalty bylaw and general administrative penalty bylaw applies, as designated therein;
